# Vendor reference clone — too large for git, available upstream at:
#   https://github.com/Xinyuan-LilyGO/LilyGo-T-SIM7080G
# The PDFs we actually need are copied into docs/ and docs/datasheets/.
docs/LilyGo-T-SIM7080G/

# Track 0 / WS-10: per-device provisioning artifacts. The NVS blob + its
# transient gen CSV carry the CLEARTEXT per-device secret — never commit.
/prov-out/

# ruflo / claude-flow runtime data — auto-generated, machine-local, not source
.claude-flow/data/

# Track 3 / hardware foundation: the Secure Boot v2 signing key + Flash
# Encryption key are CRITICAL secrets. Losing the SB key bricks the ability
# to reflash a fused board; committing it defeats Secure Boot entirely.
# Owner archives these OUTSIDE the repo. Never commit. The secure build
# profile (sdkconfig.secure) carries NO key material and IS committed.
/secure/
*.pem
flash_encryption_key.bin
secure_boot_signing_key*.pem

# Build artifacts and directories
**/build/
build/
# Custom ESP-IDF build dirs (build_fe, build_secure, etc.)
build_*/
**/build_*/
*.o
*.a
*.out
*.exe # For any host-side utilities compiled on Windows

# ESP-IDF specific build outputs
*.bin
*.elf
*.map
flasher_args.json # Generated in build directory
sdkconfig.old
sdkconfig

